        "created_at": "2015-03-30T20:44:21.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>nope, that scenario doesn't work right.</p><p>Try these changes for a better game:</p><p>1.&nbsp; Only use 5 shards.&nbsp; No matter what all shards start being carried by a citizen.</p><p>2.&nbsp; Get rid of the time limit, make the win condition 3 shards captured by either team.</p><p>3.&nbsp; The winner of scenario 1 gets 1 shard captured to start (this would be 1 of the 5 shards for the scenario)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>This lets the citizens try to run 2-3 shards to the victory point, while the heroes have to force the citizens to drop shards and then recover them to win.</p><p>Initial tests show it works at least decently, and is much better than the official scenario.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 31,
        "post_type": 1,
