      {
        "id": 116643,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-03-30T23:46:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Gislef\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/g/4af34b/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Gislef:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We'll try it.But… to repeat one question above, does the -2 move from a shard go away as soon as the holder drops the shard? Or is permanent for the entire turn once it kicks in at the beginning of the turn?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>The -2 move is applied for each shard the target is currently carrying. &nbsp;So 1 shard gives you a -2, two shards give a -4, three a -6 and zero shards no penalty.</p>\n<p>Picking up or tossing a shard mid turn would change your movement as soon as you gained or dropped a shard.</p>",
